[32m+[m[32m# AGENTS.md[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mInstructions for any coding agent (or human) working in this repo. Read this[m
[32m+[m[32mbefore editing `app.R` or anything in `modules/`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## What this project is[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA single-file-ish Shiny app (`app.R`) for plant-breeding trial analysis, plus[m
[32m+[m[32mnumbered `modules/*.R` files it sources. Two of those modules are the[m
[32m+[m[32mselection-index core:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `module_4_selection_index.R` — thin wrapper/name registry; the LPSI[m
[32m+[m[32m  (Single-Location Trial) engine and its helpers live in `app.R`,[m
[32m+[m[32m  `shared_data_validation.R`, and `advanced_analysis_extensions.R`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `module_multi_factor.R` — factorial and split-plot analysis for two or[m
[32m+[m[32m  three treatment factors.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `module_5_met.R` — the full Multi-Environment Trial engine: outlier[m
[32m+[m[32m  cleaning, LMM/ANOVA modeling, AMMI, GGE, Finlay–Wickham, ASV, integrated[m
[32m+[m[32m  multi-trait ranking, and the ADVANCE/RETEST/DISCARD decision board.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSee `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` for the full data flow and `docs/PRD.md` for scope.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Ground rules[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Don't break the module contract.** `app.R` calls specific function[m
[32m+[m[32m   names and expects specific list fields back (e.g. `result$anova_full`,[m
[32m+[m[32m   `result$met_by_trait[[trait]]$genotype_summary`). If you rename or[m
[32m+[m[32m   restructure a function's return value, grep `app.R` for every call site[m
[32m+[m[32m   and every `results$<field>` / `result$<field>` access before finishing.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Keep `id_col`, `rep_col`, and the weight/direction row labels in one[m
[32m+[m[32m   place.** They're defined once near the top of `app.R`[m
[32m+[m[32m   (`id_col`, `rep_col`, `weight_row_labels`, `direction_row_labels`,[m
[32m+[m[32m   `type_col_candidates`, `check_type_labels`). Don't hardcode `"Variety"`[m
[32m+[m[32m   or `"Rep"` elsewhere — reference these constants.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **New analysis types follow the existing five-part pattern:**[m
[32m+[m[32m   - a `run_*` function that takes the uploaded data.frame + settings and[m
[32m+[m[32m     returns a named list of result tables/plots[m
[32m+[m[32m   - an entry in `saved_results` (reactiveValues in `server()`)[m
[32m+[m[32m   - a branch in `build_export_tables()` for the xlsx export[m
[32m+[m[32m   - `nav_panel` / `conditionalPanel` wiring in the UI for "Analyze",[m
[32m+[m[32m     "Results", and "Charts"[m
[32m+[m[32m   - an entry in `analysis_method` choices and `download_all`'s[m
[32m+[m[32m     `export_names`[m
[32m+[m[32m   Match this pattern rather than inventing a parallel mechanism.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **MET-specific:** trait columns can carry per-trait `weight`, `direction`,[m
[32m+[m[32m   and `target_value` metadata (read via `make_met_data()` /[m
[32m+[m[32m   `prepare_met_trait_settings()`). Respect `trait_direction` ("Higher[m
[32m+[m[32m   better" vs "Lower better"/target-based) in any new scoring or ranking[m
[32m+[m[32m   logic — don't assume higher-is-always-better.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. **MET model type is a user choice**, not a hardcoded model. Any new MET[m
[32m+[m[32m   output should work under `"LMM"`, `"SOMMER"`, and `"ANOVA_RCBD"`, and[m
[32m+[m[32m   label estimates correctly (`BLUP` vs adjusted mean/BLUE) — see[m
[32m+[m[32m   `estimate_label` in `run_met_pipeline()`.[m
[32m+[m[32m6. **Never silently drop genotypes/environments.** Outlier filtering,[m
[32m+[m[32m   missing-check-genotype handling, and single-environment genotypes all[m
[32m+[m[32m   push human-readable strings into a `notes` vector that surfaces in the[m
[32m+[m[32m   pipeline-review output. If you add filtering, add a matching note.[m
[32m+[m[32m7. **Plots use `theme_bw()` and a small fixed palette** (e.g. `#3498DB` kept,[m
[32m+[m[32m   `#E74C3C` outlier/flag, `#2ECC71` clean/good). Match this rather than[m
[32m+[m[32m   introducing new ad hoc colors, so Charts stays visually consistent.[m
[32m+[m[32m8. **Downloads are the contract with the breeder.** Every result field that[m
[32m+[m[32m   should be exportable must be added to `build_export_tables()` — a table[m
[32m+[m[32m   only visible in the Results tab but missing from exports is a bug.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Module placement[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mShared upload and selection helpers live in `modules/shared_data_validation.R`.[m
[32m+[m[32mSelection-index extensions live in `modules/advanced_analysis_extensions.R`.[m
[32m+[m[32mKeep the naming convention (`si_*` for shared/selection-index helpers,[m
[32m+[m[32m`mf_*` for Multi-factor, and `met_*`/`si_met_*` for MET) and update[m
[32m+[m[32m`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` when adding modules.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Before you open a PR / hand back code[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Grep `app.R` for every reference to any function/field you changed[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] If you touched `run_met_pipeline()` or `build_export_tables()`, confirm[m
[32m+[m[32m      both the `LMM` and `ANOVA_RCBD` code paths still run[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] If you added a result table, confirm it's wired into: Results tab[m
[32m+[m[32m      (`conditionalPanel` + `DTOutput`), Export (`build_export_tables`), and[m
[32m+[m[32m      (if relevant) Charts[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Don't commit real breeding-trial data — use synthetic Variety/Rep/trait[m
[32m+[m[32m      data for testing[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Match existing style: base R + tidyverse pipes (`%>%`), snake_case[m
[32m+[m[32m      function names, `si_`/`met_` prefixes for module-scoped helpers[m
